  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Tag with a ball",
  "description": "All the players are inside a box of cones, each with a ball, and must keep dribbling the whole time. Two coaches are the taggers. Anyone touched, or anyone who leaves the box, is caught and stands still. A free player can rescue a caught team-mate by passing their ball between the team-mate's legs. Start and stop with the whistle and play a few minutes at a time – is everyone caught when time is up?\n\nAs a tagger: pace yourself so the players win most of the time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – then you see both the taggers and your team-mates."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to the stick when you change direction."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Help each other: rescue a caught team-mate as soon as you can."
    }
  ],
